        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Section 106 viability review mechanisms have become a standard feature of planning obligations on major residential schemes, particularly in London and high-value areas. For a housing association like Clarion/Latimer operating as both developer and RP, understanding the triggers, methodology, and financial implications of late-stage reviews is essential. These mechanisms are designed to capture increases in scheme value that occur between planning consent and practical completion, redirecting surplus profit towards additional affordable housing \u2014 either on-site units or commuted sums."
