        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The clawback calculation typically follows a defined formula in the S106 agreement. The key inputs are: (1) Actual Gross Development Value (GDV) \u2014 based on achieved sales prices and contracted affordable housing revenues; (2) Actual total development costs \u2014 including build costs, professional fees, finance, CIL, S106 obligations already met, and marketing; (3) Agreed developer return \u2014 usually expressed as a percentage of GDV (typically 15\u201320% on market housing, 6% on affordable housing); (4) The 'surplus' being the difference between actual profit and the agreed benchmark profit. The surplus is then typically shared 60/40 or 50/50 between the LPA (as additional affordable housing contribution) and the developer, subject to a cap equivalent to policy-compliant affordable housing delivery."
