        "text": "The NPPF (December 2024 revision) and the PPG on Viability make clear that policy-compliant affordable housing should be the starting expectation. However, where a Financial Viability Assessment (FVA) demonstrates that full policy compliance renders a scheme unviable, LPAs may accept a reduced affordable housing offer \u2014 but only subject to review mechanisms that protect the public interest if market conditions improve. The London Plan (Policy H5) mandates two routes: a Fast Track Route (no viability review required if \u226535% affordable housing at specified tenure split, or \u226550% on public land/industrial sites) and a Viability Tested Route where early, mid, and late-stage reviews are embedded in the S106."
